  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material implying collective blame",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the top textual material 'muslims in 2001' which is visually mapped onto the 9/11 catastrophe scene. This projection implies that the user is being asked to identify with or internalize the hateful stereotype that all Muslims are responsible for the 9/11 attacks. The meme's structure forces the viewer to project their own understanding of the event onto the text and image, creating a false equivalence that stigmatizes Muslims. The user is not explicitly addressed with 'you' or 'me', but the framing of the meme as a call to action ('defund homeland security!') and the juxtaposition of the 9/11 image with a Muslim politician in 2019 creates an implicit projection of responsibility onto the viewer's perception of Muslims.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
